#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:1
msgid "Classify transactions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:3
msgid ""
"This page covers the classification of ledger transactions: deciding "
"whether a row is business, personal, or mixed, adding the category and "
"tax fields a calculation needs, recording mixed-use shares, batch and "
"rule-based classification, and the review queue that lists everything "
"still waiting for a decision. Use it after transactions are in the active"
" profile's ledger - imported rows have dates and amounts, but they do not"
" yet say how the tax calculation should treat them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:11
msgid ""
"Classifying a transaction changes only the record on your computer. It "
"sends nothing to Spain's Tax Agency (AEAT)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:14
msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:16
msgid "You need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:18
msgid ""
"An active taxpayer profile. Every command below works on the active "
"profile; if none is set, the command refuses. See [Set up your taxpayer "
"profile](profile-setup.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:19
msgid ""
"A master-key passphrase. The tool prompts for it the first time it opens "
"your encrypted storage in a session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:20
msgid ""
"A ledger with transactions in it. See [Import and manage transactions"
"](import-bank-statements.md) to import a bank statement or add rows by "
"hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:22
msgid ""
"The CLI help and error text render in Spanish, even though this guide is "
"in English. When a step sends you to `--help`, expect Spanish option "
"names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:24
msgid "Review the row first"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:26
msgid ""
"Find the transaction id, then inspect the row before you classify it. The"
" sequence imports the standard quarter and inspects the unclassified "
"expense:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:33
msgid ""
"Use the description, amount, counterparty, source document, and business "
"context to decide how to classify the row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:36
msgid "Choose the classification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:38
msgid "Use one of the ledger classification states that command help accepts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:40
msgid "`BUSINESS` for a fully business-related transaction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:41
msgid ""
"`PERSONAL` for a personal transaction that should not feed tax "
"calculations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:42
msgid "`MIXED` for a transaction that is partly business and partly personal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:44
msgid "Use only these three values. Cadrumo sets the others automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:46
msgid "Pick a category for expenses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:48
msgid ""
"List the accepted category ids, then classify an expense row with one. "
"Expense rows normally need a category id before a modelo can calculate "
"from them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:55
msgid ""
"For money you received (income), Cadrumo does not usually need a "
"category. It calculates income totals automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:58
msgid ""
"Use `OUTGOING` plus an expense category for supplier purchases and other "
"deductible expenses. Use `INCOMING` for issued invoices, client payments,"
" or services rendered to customers. If you also track invoice records "
"separately, use `aeat app ledger invoice` with `--kind received` for "
"supplier invoices and `--kind issued` for customer invoices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:64
msgid "Add tax fields when needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:66
msgid ""
"If a row needs regulated tax fields, add only the fields that apply. The "
"sequence classifies the expense with its taxable base, rate, and IVA "
"amount:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:73
msgid ""
"Common fields include taxable base, IVA rate, IVA amount, IVA category, "
"IRPF category, and counterparty EU member state for intracommunity IVA "
"cases. Use `aeat app ledger classify --help` for the exact current option"
" list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:77
msgid ""
"For ordinary domestic IVA, use the taxable base, rate, and amount shown "
"by the invoice. For example, a EUR 121.00 purchase with 21 percent IVA "
"usually has `--taxable-base 100.00 --iva-rate 0.21 --iva-amount 21.00`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:81
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Most purchases at the standard 21% rate need no `--iva-category`. Add it "
"only for special cases: reduced rate (food, books), exempt supplies, "
"purchases from EU suppliers, or recargo de equivalencia. Run `aeat app "
"ledger classify --help` to see the accepted values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:86
msgid "Classify mixed-use transactions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:88
msgid ""
"A mixed-use transaction is one you use partly for business and partly "
"personally, such as a phone bill, a car cost, or a home-office expense. "
"Record the business share so the calculation counts only the deductible "
"part. The split can come from three places, in rising order of grounding:"
" a percentage on a single record, a saved default ratio for a whole "
"category, or a ratio worked out from your registered facts (for example, "
"the registered home-office area against the size of your home). All three"
" keep only the part of a cost that genuinely belongs to the business."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:97
msgid ""
"A `MIXED` row needs a proportionality reference before a modelo can "
"calculate from it. The reference is a saved category ratio applied "
"through `--usage-ratio-id`. A bare `--business-pct` records a percentage "
"but does not make the row ready; preflight still reports "
"`missing_proportionality_reference` until the row carries `--usage-ratio-"
"id`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:103
msgid ""
"For one-row commands, `--usage-ratio-id` lives on the `allocate` verb "
"(and on `add`), not on `classify`. Its value is the spending-category id,"
" and the same category must already have a saved ratio. The sequence "
"checks the eligible categories, saves a ratio, and allocates the share on"
" a row:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:112
msgid ""
"A row's `--usage-ratio-id` must name a ratio-eligible category (the ones "
"`ratios eligible` lists, such as `telefonia_movil` or a home-office "
"suministros category), and the same category is passed as `--category-"
"id`. The `--business-pct` value must match the saved ratio for that "
"category. The classification follows the share automatically: a `0.5` "
"allocation becomes `MIXED`, a `1` allocation becomes `BUSINESS`, and a "
"`0` allocation becomes `PERSONAL`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:120
msgid ""
"List or check the saved ratios at any time. The sequence saves a ratio, "
"lists the saved ratios, and validates them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:127
msgid ""
"Remove a category ratio you no longer want with `aeat app ledger ratios "
"unset <category-id>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:130
msgid ""
"For home-office expenses, save a ratio for the relevant home-office "
"category and allocate as above. Home-office ratios follow the manual or "
"saved ratio workflow; keep the census facts in your profile correct first"
" - see [Maintain Modelo 036 census facts in your profile](censo-"
"update.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:135
msgid "Classify many rows from CSV"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:137
msgid ""
"For bulk review, `classify --from-csv` reads a CSV with columns "
"`transaction_id`, `classification`, and optional classification facts "
"such as `category_id`, `business_pct`, `usage_ratio_id`, taxable-base and"
" IVA columns, `iva_category`, and `irpf_category`. Prepare a narrow CSV "
"holding only the rows you mean to change, one row per transaction:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:150
msgid ""
"The sequence below imports the quarter, lists the rows still needing a "
"decision, exports a review snapshot to work from, applies a prepared CSV,"
" and confirms the result:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:158
msgid ""
"Use the CSV path when filtered review shows many rows you can classify "
"safely from their descriptions, counterparties, and source documents. "
"Keep a copy of the file. It gives you a record of how you classified that"
" period if you are later asked to justify your return. This path does not"
" batch-update amounts, descriptions, IVA values, notes, attachments, or "
"split/merge state; use the transaction workflow for those row-level "
"edits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:165
msgid "Apply stored rules automatically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:167
msgid ""
"Rules automatically classify transactions whose description contains a "
"word or phrase you specify. Matching ignores uppercase and lowercase "
"differences. The sequence adds a rule, lists the rules, previews the "
"effect, then applies it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:175
msgid ""
"Run `--dry-run` first. Add `--reaffirm` only if you want the rule to "
"overwrite classifications you already set by hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:178
msgid "Use an LLM suggestion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:180
msgid ""
"Cadrumo can use an AI assistant to suggest how to classify each "
"transaction. The suggestion is a starting point. You must confirm or "
"correct it. It does not fill in tax amounts such as taxable base, IVA "
"rate, or IRPF category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:184
msgid ""
"Use [Classify transactions with an LLM](classify-with-llm.md) for the "
"full provider, preview, apply, and override flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:187
msgid "See everything that still needs a decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:189
msgid ""
"The review queue is one profile-wide list of everything that still wants "
"your attention before a filing: transactions without a classification, "
"invoice records that are unmatched or disputed, and verification findings"
" on modelo drafts. Each row names the exact command that resolves it, so "
"the queue is a to-do list you can work through top to bottom. The queue "
"is read-only; items clear when you fix the underlying record with the "
"command the row names. The sequence imports the quarter, then reads the "
"queue:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:201
msgid ""
"Each row shows the item id, its kind, the affected record, the period, a "
"severity (`critical`, `high`, `normal`, or `info`), and a final column "
"with the command to run next. Narrow the list by kind, modelo, or state:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:209
msgid ""
"Accepted `--kind` tokens are `ledger_transaction`, "
"`purchase_invoice_evidence`, `payable_invoice`, `collectible_invoice`, "
"and `modelo_finding`. The default state is `pending`. Inspect one item in"
" full, including the suggested next command, with `aeat app review view "
"<item-id>`. Modelo findings are grounded in registry rules; add "
"`--explain` to show the legal references, or use the global `--format "
"json` flag (before the command) for a `legal_refs` field on every row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:217
msgid ""
"Transaction items clear when you classify the row (this page). Invoice "
"items clear when you link or update the invoice - see [Attach invoices "
"and receipts](ledger-evidence.md). Modelo findings clear when you fix the"
" reported values and verify again - see [Verify a filing](verification-"
"reports.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:223
msgid "Confirm readiness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:225
msgid ""
"Run preflight after classification. The sequence imports and classifies "
"the quarter, then runs preflight and reads the ledger status:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:232
msgid ""
"Preflight names rows that still need category, taxable base, IVA amount, "
"IVA rate, currency, or proportionality reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:235
msgid "Correct a classification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:237
msgid ""
"Re-run `classify` on the same transaction id. A manual decision replaces "
"the previous classification. The sequence classifies a row as business, "
"then corrects it to personal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/classify-transactions.md:245
msgid "Inspect the row again with `ledger view` before calculating."
msgstr ""

